editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:17:## 1. Entry state and ending state (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:19:### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:24:- **Objects/accounts:** the tarred-canvas kit case, strap, cord knotted at the fives, unused stake 32 with stroke/bar and bright turned point, and mallet are at the back-room table; the dead man's ledger is shut beside them. Three boxes stand at the warm wall. The cart-and-gelding reserve remains sealed under five thumbprints in the third box, separate from the 96-mark living purse. The Fallow hundred and Stair 300 remain in Pike's box, unmarked and not crew-payable debts. The ferryman is owed 60 yards of four-strand rope, not wanted before the thaw. The forty-mark axe-head fence is taken and not begun. Teague forfeited the four-mark weir slip. The six-mark back room is paid through the cold term; hearth space is covered by standing-money. Two westbound letters cost one copper apiece. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:32:### Ending (source Ch24, dawn of the 308th; must hand off to Book 9)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:41:- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. [OWNER-pending #54] Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "After the next thaw. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:49:## 2. The spine — every major source event, in order (all KEEP)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:88:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] speaks to the six for the first time.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. [OWNER-pending #54] Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
