editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:441:- **C4 — The grandmother.** The universe ledger lists "Hesk's grandmother" as the owner of the straightedge saying. Book 7 edition chapter 60's note (chapter-60.md:67) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11] ("Your grandmother said…") and S17/S24 make her **Cael's** grandmother, Hesk's late wife. **Edition follows the prose.** The ledger line is a slip.
