editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:295:## AFTER MOVEMENT 3 — chapters 13–19, days 278–281 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:297:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:302:- **Protected (speakers):** "Carters declare, on the ice." (the factor, unnamed, no pronoun); "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe," (Seln — the plan quotes only this clause; the source's fuller sentence contradicts the staging and was not restored); the wall lesson (Vastin) / "You do now," (Cael) / "I know fields…" (Vastin); the log verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:311:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:312:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (3 tracked passages, none dense; probe 2% / 15%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 102 exact fixes). Coordinator rulings against the audit, after checking the source and the locked Book 7: the cut's staging, the Ember use and the count of thirty-two KEPT (BOOK_MAP §8: private staging the author owns; the audit's 39 re-staging fixes declined); Oryn's past KEPT; Cael's touch of the page KEPT; the slip left as the packet quotes it; "every bar of a fence" KEPT (Book 7 ch58). Accepted from the audit: the six markers' speakers (two filled with the plan's own clause only); the loads for Movement 4; no fifth place or number; no second calendar; the remark's hand unidentified. Eleven fixes applied by the coordinator; the rest recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:314:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:331:- **The abstracts, read in daylight.** Karis counted every row twice and had each counted again; **no figure for any row is printed**. **She gives no number of places.** She sorted the sheets by their sign-groups, matched **four** to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double), and will not call the unmatched groups places until a sign can be read (17:27–39). **Five columns:** the day, in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments*; and the anomaly. No radius of the four has changed by a stride in six years; four surveyors by their figures; three clerks' hands. The fourth column reads *Cord true. Edge true. Level true.* on every sheet. The three oldest rows have a ruled space at the foot headed *Remarks*, empty but once: **the Stair's sheet in the fourth row carries the protected four words, in a hand that is none of the three clerks'; Karis laid the dead man's ledger beside it and will not swear to the hand either way.** From the next year's printing the space is gone. Brom counts the three findings on his fingers (17:61, 17:77, 17:139).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:342:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:377:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:391:## AFTER MOVEMENT 4 — chapters 20–26, days 281–284 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:393:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:396:- **The reading inward (the 281st): the fourth and fifth self-readings**, with Tide, ROUND the still place and never in; **not counted** ("Myself, twice: not counted, as before"); a palm on a gatepost while it was open is a trial. Finding (protected): "He had been putting a cord on a stone and writing down *no length*." — the tenth feels only what flows; where nothing flows it returns nothing, and that nothing is the instrument's limit, not a finding about the place (a gatepost and the middle of himself come back alike). **He needs an instrument for what does not move.** He read Oryn's order for the leave he wanted, has logged that, and **owes her the telling at the mill before anything else is said**. Lira asked and is entered as having asked. **Deployment since the Line: thirty-two; ten fragments; none acquired.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:397:- **Vastin and Cael at the three-mile post.** Vastin SAT for the first time since the cut, of his own choosing, where he could not rise without Cael's arm. "I read your file" (no span of years). Cael: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." (protected, Cael's). **Why he declined** (the author's, amended to locked Book 6): the case shown him at Ostrand is the true and causal reason — the office had shown him what it did with honest readings; and privately part of him was relieved never to learn what a plate would say (a second silence would have been turned on Cael; a plate that lit would have been turned on nine thousand of his own readings). A sound act, and glad of it for a bad reason. **What Cael gave him:** that the place has been read twice that day with "the one thing I've got that reads", and nothing came back because that thing only feels what moves. NOT what reads, nor fragments, the mechanism, the date. Vastin did not ask. "It is a place where two people can stand": ground, not friendship. The S7 log verbatim ("color" stands).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:398:- **Treswick (the 282nd).** The grey bridge on five piers is of dark, dry-laid stone with no mortar and is OLDER than the walls (Karis, from the masons' fitting of the pale stone to it); the same dark stone is the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the frame of the iron door. The outer gate: one keeper counts feet on a bead-frame ("Six"); another writes only loads that come on wheels to be sold. **No name of the six was written.** The outer district works by brokers' slate boards and counted labour: cards with a coloured edge (blue to the second wall, buff to the third) carry a figure, are counted in with a pen and torn at each gate, and are good for the day named. **Iron passes the second wall by right, Bronze the third** — on a certificate that is read out and WRITTEN. The smith's two forges (charcoal; an Ember's held bed for a horse with a blue band): Brom, "They shoe by the tier." (protected). The rope-walk: sixty yards of four-strand priced (no figure printed) and to be bought going out; the Lowmarch debt stands. **The inn with two doors** (the painted door has a book; the yard half-door takes money): the long loft over the stable for a week from the 282nd, the pot at dusk, seven bowls; two marks paid; **purse 136**. Lira hung a blanket over the loft's uphill window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:400:- **Seln's report (the 282nd night):** the old town stands on a quarry cut from inside; the lower archive is behind one iron door in the undercroft beneath the registry's yard; a practitioner registered under historical studies has standing entry by the week and may have matter brought down; **"Rune Path. Bronze."**; one clerk keeps the provision's book, which has had one name in it; the form has a line for the matter, a line for its bearer (one), and **a line for hands, entered by count**. Protected: Karis "Four hands." / Seln "Four… By count." / Lira "Four hands," … "I've two." / Cael wrote: *Entered by count. That's the door.* The S8 close verbatim (Cael; Karis), with OWNER-pending #53 ("four years and a hearing") as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:401:- **Cleon at noon (the 283rd)**, at the cook-house against the second wall: he looked at one sheet from its foot upward. Protected: "Off floors," (Cleon) / "Fused. Grey. No join. Three of them. I copied every mark on all three. Fifty-two sheets," (Karis) / "Fifty-two sheets," (Cleon). His terms: not on a counter; all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is not said aloud); **not a word of what she thinks they are until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He gave a buff-edged card for the 284th at the second bell. He never looked at Cael. He stopped a step late on the paving. **His Path has not been shown.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:402:- **The 284th.** Seln is NOT on the count (a clerk might know his face; somebody must watch the door). **Vastin said "Yes" before a mouth was open** and is the fourth hand. Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; **Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands**. Both upper keepers counted ("One, and four") and tore a corner; the way to the yard goes by the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window** — never across the square. **Cael did not set foot on the square or its steps and did not look at the crown; Lira kept the same discipline unasked** and walked between him and each alley's end. **Lira's ladder did not pull** ("It's a hill with a tax on it"); protected: "Four hands," (Lira) / "Four." (Cael) / "Right." (Lira); the S9 log verbatim. Her registry paper stayed in her coat. **The yard clerk (unnamed) asked nothing and wrote *four*.** None of the four restricted names has been written; the asset-restriction is still pending.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:407:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:408:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol), with the audit instructed to separate protected text and plan facts from the source's staging: editorial; cold read; source-distance (2 tracked passages, both in ch26; probe 2% / 10%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (bounded line repair; 10 exact fixes; every piece of the author's staging and city mechanics ratified). Nine fixes applied by the coordinator (five markers restored whole with speakers; the full inward-finding sentence; Shadow's ordinal; Cleon's lamp term; the parapet exchange moved); the tenth (the weighting of Vastin's refusal against Book 6) recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:410:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:425:- **Cleon, as seen.** Not tall; grey hair cut short and badly; a coat the colour of dust; round shoulders; square pale hands with the nails pared to the quick; red-rimmed wet eyes, which he keeps shut while he eats; a voice "like a hinge". He looks at a sheet from its foot upward. He eats at the counter's end by the yard door at noon and goes down within the hour. **Cael knows him for Cleon at the counter** (the name said at a spring) and reads it once, written, at the head of the card in Lira's hands on the 283rd; nobody says it aloud. Karis told him at the counter what the floors are (the protected line: fused, grey, no join; three of them; fifty-two sheets), so his questions after it are of method only (rubbed or drawn; what light; which edge north; how far apart). **His terms (mine, one amended by the audit):** not on a counter; all of them, not a choice; they come down to him and he does not come up; his card, written at the counter (the matter; its bearer, one; hands, a figure), good for the next day only, at the second bell; no names given or wanted; not a word of what she thinks they are until he has looked; **one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says, and no other carried light or fire of anybody's** (a light already burning below is not excluded). He pushed her sheet back without touching it. He left by the street door and stopped a full stride beyond it for three breaths. **He never looked toward the yard.** The Path is not shown; only that he rests his eyes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:434:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:455:**Cleon.** Named by the narration in chapter 24 (at the counter, and in the tags of the protected exchange) and once in chapter 26; never said aloud by anybody in this movement; Cael has read the name on the card. Rune Path, Bronze, by Seln's report only. He has set terms, written a card, and pulled the iron to. He has taken no notice of Cael. He has been told what the floors are (fused, grey, no join; three; fifty-two sheets) and nothing of what the sheets are thought to mean.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:465:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:478:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (a bounded line repair; nothing re-staged): the nine coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (the boulder image made to agree with "*no length*"; Karis looks at three boxes and a case before "Four hands."; the cook-house questions after the restored exchange are of method only; "Four." given to Cael at the parapet); Vastin's refusal recomposed to locked Book 6 (the Ostrand case stated as the cause, twice, and not taken back; beside it "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one"; entered "on a form which has no line for why"); the two tracked passages in ch26 re-ordered (Lira prices the ladder aloud and shoulders the box before Cael understands; the clerk writes *four* and blots it before he looks at a face, then opens the door, looks at Vastin, opens his mouth and shuts it); Wind's ceiling removed; **Cleon's name comes to Cael at the cook-house counter and is then read on the card — nobody has said it aloud**; second tellings of the name-versus-count idea trimmed. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; both tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (161 days since the last self-reading; four days since the board; 282 days since the first sill; Oryn's gates). One punctuation fix applied by the coordinator (a broken dialogue join in ch21). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,179 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (12 protected). Purse 136 marks; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; the forenoon of day 284, inside the iron door under Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:481:## AFTER MOVEMENT 5 — chapters 27–33, days 284–290 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:483:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:486:- **Cleon.** Protected, all his: "I know that hand." (of the Hall's fourth sheet); "Being believed — … It's the end of being able to be wrong."; "Give me a week." (the 284th); "They're orders."; the two-part limit ("I can tell you these are orders. I can't tell you what they order…"; "It doesn't work on a river, and it doesn't work on a man, and it doesn't work on a tree… It costs me my eyes for an hour after and nothing else."); "Same make."; and the 287th close ("documentation… built the same way twice… never once slept well since."), in which he uses Karis's name (he heard Brom say it). Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." **His Path has been shown from OUTSIDE only**: he looks at a made thing from its foot upward, without blinking, and says which signs BEAR (white), which are CARRIED (black) and which are NOTHING (red, packing); his plank's four rows are the same lines as rows on the Hall's fourth, the Stair's ninth and twenty-first, and the Ring's sixth sheets. **On the 287th he set his own week to run from that day to the 293rd, with everything else put aside**; at its end every sheet goes up. The bundle on his shelf ("Paper. Not stone.", from the same shelf as the plank) is tied and unread. He has not noticed Cael, who holds his lamp ("a hand to the left"); he knows nothing of the alley, the fragments or the mechanism.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:488:- **The yard door, the 285th.** The clerk's form had no line for matter that had gone up and come back; he asked one question ("The same?") and was about to send up for the under-registrar. **Vastin gave his old name, rank and office aloud** (protected: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —"); the clerk's pen came up and **wrote nothing of it**. **Seln, posing as a porter on the hatch's bench, answered truthfully** (protected, whole: "He's on the count. Four hands, same as yesterday, entered by the practitioner and answered for by her, and the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was. The researcher's at your counter and she'll want to be told we're through,"). The clerk wrote *The same* and *four*, and has done so each day since. **The cost: a Treswick registry clerk now knows Seln's face and voice.** "I'm sorry." (Vastin) / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." (Seln). Seln watches from the roof above the cut's head from then on. No restricted name has been written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:491:- **Vastin** went toward the lamp four times on the 287th, twice on the 288th, not at all on the 290th. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:493:- **THE ELEVENTH.** In that quiet minute **Cael acquired Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin** — it did not fill, it *set*, "as a post is stood in its hole"; its prompt is *This far?*; he has told it no each time. **Not deployed. Not told to Vastin.** The protected lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics (not a system block): "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. … Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh." **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line: thirty-two.** Vastin: "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered…" ("it" is what Cael is, which he could not read) / "It's entered," — and Cael has entered more than the man knows: **a debt he cannot yet pay** ("Not told. I can't tell the taking without telling the rest, and the rest is six people's"). Lira has read the log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:498:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:499:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch27 scene 2; probe 2% / 14%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES; ten exact fixes; all nineteen author flags and every minted item KEPT). Eight applied by the coordinator (five markers restored whole with speakers — two of Cleon's had been staged as Karis's — and three joins). Two DECLINED: the audit wanted the eleventh's lines printed as system text under a FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading; the protected unit is Cael's own cataloguing (it names Vastin and says "Eleventh"; the twelfth says "me"), so the author's frame stands and the coordinator set the unit in italics instead of a code fence. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:501:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:515:- **Cleon's week (as repaired).** On the 284th, from his chair, with his eyes shut, Cleon said what being believed was to him (protected) and then asked for a week (protected: "Give me a week."); Karis asked the five for the same week in her own words ("I should like his week"), and Cael said that it was hers. On the 287th he re-set it: he had spent the half of the first on his own page, which he read every morning before he would look at hers; that is put by, and the week is his, from that day, with nothing else on the desk. At its end every sheet goes up and the clerk writes that it is gone (he will not have matter lying a month under *the same*). Its seventh day is the 293rd; three days are left after the 290th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:529:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:558:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:573:**Movement 5 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Same-author repair r1 (ch27–31; ch32–33 untouched apart from the eleventh's lines set in italics): the eight coordinator-applied fixes kept and re-joined — **ch27's scene at the Hall's table now turns on Cleon** (Cael's "Then what is it?" goes to Karis, who does not answer; Cleon, eyes shut at his desk, says the "Being believed" unit to himself in the hearing of five; Karis tells Brom who has believed him; Cleon opens his eyes for "Give me a week."; **Karis then asks the five in her own words — "I should like his week" — and Cael says it is hers**); ch30, Cleon re-sets his own week from the 287th (half the first went on his own page each morning; that is put by); ch31's opening keeps only her side of being believed; Seln's line at the hatch whole, with the narration noting that he said nothing that was not in the clerk's own book or at his ledge, "and he had said *we*, which lay in no book at all"; Cleon's close whole with the author's joins. The tracked passage re-ordered (Cleon gives his table orders over his shoulder with his finger on his line; when Cael looks again the chair is empty and the leaf lies face up, unmarked); two physical anchors in the cipher proof; restated method compressed; first-use anchors added. Sol recheck: **CLOSE, no line fixes**; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the coordinator's ruling on the eleventh's lines (Cael's own cataloguing, in italics, not a system block) treated as settled and consistent on the page. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,987 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (17 protected). Purse 134 marks; deployment thirty-two; **eleven fragments**; the night of day 290, in the loft at Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:576:## AFTER MOVEMENT 6 — chapters 34–40, days 291–293 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:578:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:580:- **THE TWELFTH.** On the 291st, at Cleon's "There," (his finger at the end of the Stair's fifth row), **Cael acquired Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** — "given, not taken": it did not pour or set, it *turned*. Protected, Cleon's, in this order: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair."; then Karis's "The strata lean too."; then "There,". The protected lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics (never a system block): "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean … Deployment: none. Twelfth." with *He looked away. Kept.* and *Not a man.* **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line: thirty-two.** It gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*); it costs the eyes afterward (paid on the stair, Vastin guiding him); made things only.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:582:- **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira first, on the stair ("Twelfth. His. Lean."); Brom, Karis and Seln; **Cleon, told by Cael at the bell, in the order he has it** ("You did what." / "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's — " / "No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you."). Cleon knows how this ONE fragment came and nothing of any other. **Not Oryn; not Vastin.** **Cleon's warning** (protected, whole: "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that … Everything I read is *made* … If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — … Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it.") is known to Cael and Cleon only and **is in no book**. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered." Cleon looks away from the boy on purpose from then on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:585:- **The 292nd.** Hesk's parcel (the dividers; **Hesk's note, verbatim**) came by the carrier with the cut hat; Cael has not opened them on any distance. The dinner: four marks, seven cups poured and two kept under saucers (Karis; Oryn): **purse 130**. Protected, **Cael's, said to Vastin**: "Out here you count who's owed a seat … It's a different ledger." Seln read a slip, burned it and said "Closed."; what was on it is not given. **The first inventory written inside walls.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:588:- **THE LEAF (the 293rd).** A single leaf of horn-coloured skin between beech boards from the bundle on Cleon's shelf; twenty-six lines on its face in the floors' letters; a list on its back, **not gone into**; a place four or five letters wide scraped pale, with one upright stroke left. **Karis read it aloud ONCE** (protected, whole, in the record's voice: "In the years of the unmaking … that they should not come again."). Her one account: "It's a title, not a name; the name's gone."; ***The Architect*** (spoken once, by her; the word on Vastin's copied page); by the year at the leaf's head, in the old town's count, **about four hundred years ago**; the purpose is the un-bound. "Older," she said. "Made. Us." **Heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; nobody who heard it quotes it.** Karis has all twenty-three letters (her first word that was not a number was *and*; the covered six-sign word was *set*).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:589:- **The chronicle.** Under the lower board, a later year-book of the town on paper. Karis read one line out (protected: "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —") and stopped at a thumb-wide hole: "I am not going to read into a hole." "Marked." (Karis) / "Marked." (Cleon). **The hole stays a hole: no gloss, no guess, no second source, and nobody speaks of the line again.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:590:- **Two pages.** Vastin reached once aloud (protected: "The apparatus … And the mark that is given at the kindling — ") and Karis stopped him: evidence on one page, inference on another, and the second page has nothing on it. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, the sigils, the plates, the Arbiters or the stations**; *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure* do not occur. Karis made two copies with the gap ruled as an empty box; the fair one is in Cael's coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:591:- **The street and the fire (the 293rd evening).** At the inner stair's head Cael read Karis's page **the right way up** for the first time ("There was no desk on the other side of this."). He told Seln on the carts' street; **both lines are Seln's**: "Made." / "For a kind." At the yard fire Lira read first; the fixed order held; Cleon came above ground once, ate half a bowl and undertook that the skin stays under his hand and goes to no counter. **Seln:** the case is on his chest, **shut**, its contents unnamed; "I'll keep it a while longer." (a decision, not a disclosure; no count of years is printed here — closed chapter 18 says twelve). **Vastin** (protected): "I believed it was imperfect." / "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." / "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire."; to Lira's "His?": "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." / "I would have." Brom priced it and withheld a verdict ("I'd want to hear the other side"): **the record's fear is reported and not endorsed.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:592:- **POLE TWO.** Cael, on his feet at the fire (protected): "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me … It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." / "I happened anyway." Lira: "Yeah." / "Now what." Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is … There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." / "I want to stand in the middle of it." **It is not in the log.** "Four hundred" stands exactly twice in the movement (Karis's account; pole two).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:597:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:598:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (5 tracked passages; probe 3% / 18%; the two capacity-failed lanes were relaunched and ran); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR, bounded; thirty-seven exact fixes; all thirteen author flags KEPT). **Seventeen applied by the coordinator**: the sixteen marker restorations and the light. **Four AMENDED to the plan's own pieces** where the source's fuller wording clashed with this edition (Cleon's speech uses a term the edition never has; the leaf's aside contradicts the live first reading; the title sentence would have doubled *The Architect*; Seln's speech put the case on his back for four years against closed chapter 18's chest and twelve). **Twenty DECLINED**: fix 17, and fixes 18–36 as a class (the audit read "does not turn unbidden until Millrace" as forbidding the outward lean that the same packet prescribes). The editorial read's "marked, not read" objection to the chronicle is DECLINED (the line is protected text that must stand once; the hole is what is not read). Speakers the author's staging had left open and the audit pinned: the cups line is Cael's; both street lines are Seln's; "there" is Cleon's. **Repair r1 by the same author (claude-opus-5-5): thirteen joins written, five tracked chains broken, two orientation cues; Sol recheck CLOSE with no line fixes.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:600:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:619:- **The meal.** Brom's ruling ("A parcel's come the breadth of the country to a hayloft, and found it. That's eaten on"); four marks at the half-door; the lower room; a goose, a pie, a white loaf, baked apples, cider; seven cups poured, two kept under saucers (Karis, above with her letters; Oryn). **Purse 130.** **(r1) The cups line is Cael's:** Vastin says of the two absent women, "I have kept the count at a great many boards. I should have struck both"; Cael answers with the protected line, across the table; Vastin: "I see that it is… I was never shown the book." Brom fills his cup. (Vastin's remark over the dividers and Brom's "That's so" are cut.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:628:- **The street (r1).** Both protected lines are Seln's. Cael, asked not to say the leaf over, gives two sentences "as a carter gives a load": "It's one man's work. All of it; the tiers, and the rest. He says so himself." / "Made," / "And he says who it was built against. It wasn't a house. It was a sort of people." / "For a kind." Seln says nothing for ten paces, with his left hand on the strap; then, "I have had two sentences, which is as much as I trust from any mouth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:633:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:666:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:680:**Movement 6 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Chapters 34–40, days 291–293, 36,152 words. Same-author repair r1; Sol recheck (gpt-5.6-sol, 372k tokens): CLOSE, no line fixes — every protected unit whole, once and on the right speaker; all thirteen former joins judged the author's own and source-distant; the five tracked passages RESOLVED; overlap 0 unprotected / 27 protected; gates 0; every chapter inside the three working ranges; listening pass on all seven chapters. Recheck rulings on repair-minted items, all KEEP: Cleon's "Sits. The lot of it sits." classifies the leaf's visible FACE as a record and makes no claim about the unread back; Vastin's fire join is supported clause by clause in closed text; Cael sits on the unused bucket before Vastin speaks and rises for pole two. Text is closed for the movement, NOT locked: the book's completion pass (whole-arc read, texture lanes, listening proof) may still touch it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:683:## AFTER MOVEMENT 7 — chapters 41–46, days 294–299 (drafted 2026-10-12, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:685:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:687:- **The 294th: the list of parts.** Cleon turned the skin between boards; its back is paler, scored and not inked, **nine short lines, a thing and its number to each**. Karis can spell all nine and turn four (the four things the face says were made); the other five are spelled and unturned, and **she has said none of the numbers aloud**. **The fourth line is the mark's:** the word for the mark is what bears; two runs hang from it LEVEL (those who are kindled; and a six-sign word in the scraped-thin place), and after both the number *three*. Cleon made a second copy, drawn and not read, and gave it to Karis ("Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line."). The fifty-two sheets were counted into three boxes under two hands, K. and V. The clerk wrote *Withdrawn by its bearer* and *four* and ruled the account off. Protected, Cleon's, at the iron door: "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans." **He is not above ground and did not look at Cael.** This edition has no noun "bearer" for a sign (signs bear, are carried, or are nothing).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:690:- **The shoulder hold.** The factor offered twenty at each first frost to the five; Brom declined ("We're walking east"). Protected: "He said you'd say that." — **"he" is Teague**, who took the salt up himself, asked the factor twice how long the wall stood and whether its maker moved, and built his term on the answer. (The draft's offer of a seat at the hold's fire for Vastin was CUT: where he belongs is not this book's to open.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:691:- **The cut revisited (the 296th).** Protected, **Vastin's**: "Here."; he stood on the bound leg once with the stick off the ground; Brom, low: "Held,"; "Two words," … "Both of them ours." (Vastin's, one speech — the two words are "Here" and "Held"); Cael: "Noted" — the first time he has given that word to this man. **A horseman kept a mile behind from the cut to the dark; a riderless horse stood in the alders on the western bank on the 297th.** No face, no name; Seln "can put it no higher". Nothing was seen east of the river.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:692:- **Lowmarch (the 297th).** Pike's twelfth line is the clearance (*Eight. Twenty; paid.*); the thirteenth, protected: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*, with price and outcome left empty and said to be empty. **Cael read it the right way up, from Pike's side of the bench.** Pike put a DAY against the season line (nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated."). **Teague's term, taken as a contract** (protected: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." — all Teague's): **ten on the count — Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow, the young one; NEITHER healer**; shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's** (Cael: "It's yours. I'd have asked you to take it."); the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall has a month on it and is not stood before the month is out. No hand was offered; the cloth still reads first and eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:694:- **Force SEEN, not acquired (the 298th, first light).** Teague lined heel, knee, hip, shoulder and palm from an ash root to a sunk salt cart and put it a body's length; the recoil came back down the same line to the wrist (a click heard at twenty strides); the young one's cloth; the old woman's board. Protected, Teague's: "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." **Nothing came. Twelve. Thirty-two.** The two crews walked the meadow in file to four hand-signs (*stand*, *seen*, *come on*, *nothing*); no drill under a wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:696:- **THE GRADE (the 298th).** By laying Cleon's drawn copy on her own, Karis has four of the six signs: the word is ***set***. The fourth line: the mark, over those who are kindled and what is set; three. **Three marks:** a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY — no sheet carries it; no first-tier site appears); a stroke with one bar (stake thirty-two, the dead surveyor's book, every sheet of the four places); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a FIFTH place). Protected, Karis's: "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is."; "Somebody laid them down in order"; "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." **Ages, each counted from the office's first sheet for the place: the Fallow sixty-one, the Stair ninety-four, the Hall a hundred and thirty-eight, the place behind the iron two hundred and six**; the fifth place has two unread signs where its figure should be ("older than two hundred and six", no figure). The paper says how long ago a first sheet was drawn and nothing of who walked there since. **Vastin's first "Noted."** Protected, Teague's: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going." Hesk's dividers were **opened by Karis on Cael's loan** ("They're lent. I'll not open them."): the office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths are unsaid. Stake thirty-two is back in the tarred case, never driven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:697:- **The log of the 298th** (protected, whole, once; the grandmother is Cael's, Hesk's late wife): "Karis cracked the grade … Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." **"Four hundred" stands nowhere else in the movement**; the centuries and the figure are Cael's own inference, put on his own page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:698:- **Millrace (the 298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." (the woman with the net, as in Book 7) / "I know." (Oryn). Oryn to Vastin: "Stand there."; he stood an hour without a clause. Protected: "Nineteen days," (Vastin) / "Then it's eleven more." (Oryn). Oryn's terms: three holds owed yet on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route."; on nobody's count. "Sixth chair." (Lira) / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." (Oryn); she sat. **Readings, each asked first:** Brom's LEFT shoulder mended (a quarter-hour; she was grey), the right re-tied shorter by the older healer ("That'll do"); Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced." — "It's an arm."); Karis's palm ("Who sewed this." — the seven stitches drawn; "Write. Don't lean."); Vastin's knee — he told her of the alley wall himself; "It held in a cut," (Oryn); new linen and two laths; **the month stands as counted**; "Noted," (Vastin) / "That's new." (Oryn) / "It's a useful word." (Vastin) / "It's his." (Oryn). **Purse 127** (meal and a flitch, one mark).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:700:- **THE DEEP READING.** "May I?" / "Yes." Forty minutes, to her own floor; she found the eleventh ("stands in the stream like a post") and the twelfth ("a little flat thing behind your eyes") unprompted; her current went round the still place from every side. **At about the three hundredth breath the twelfth turned inward, unbidden: *Still.* Then *Set.*** He kept his jaw and hands loose and did not let the next word come. Oryn felt only "Something turned over … out at the edge of you. One of yours, in its sleep," and dismissed it. **Her finding, protected, whole:** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." **The two findings do not agree, and the two words are told to NO ONE** — not Oryn, not Lira. Lira offered the leaf; protected: "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf" … "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." **Oryn has not heard the leaf.** The eyes paid in the dark. Lira knows that something unasked came and has said that she will wait; the log gives four reasons for writing nothing ("Four is not mine to write") and the ruling *hold*. **Cleon's warning "has begun to lean".**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:705:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:706:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial 316k; cold 98k; source-distance 190k (2 tracked passages; probe 1% / 12%); plan / canon / protected-text audit 744k tokens (REPAIR; seventy-six exact fixes). **Twenty-five applied by the coordinator** (the sixteen marker restorations, minimal, with the source's speakers; two sign-nouns; a broken join; three thaw intervals; the factor's seat cut), five of them amended. **Fifty-one DECLINED:** Vastin made to walk the whole road (the audit did not weigh closed Movement 6's knee); the ages re-derived from a printed date (date subtraction is reserved to the unspoken sum; the author softens the corner figure's claim instead); the Millrace count given to a "ford-keeper" (the woman with the net is locked Book 7's); the night exchange with Lira cut whole (only "You went stiff" is wrong; the author re-grounds it); "Twelve. And a mule." taken from Seln. **Repair r1 by the same author (claude-opus-5-5): seven joins written, the ages passage softened, Lira's knowledge re-grounded in his eyes, two tracked chains broken, a referent pass; Sol recheck CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES (two, both applied).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:708:### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:727:- **Pike (44:101–163).** The twelfth line: *Clearance; the cut below the shoulder hold. Eight. Twenty; paid.* The thirteenth is the protected line, its last two columns empty and said to be empty. **The season line is dated:** a day in its ruled space by his own book's reckoning, nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated." **As repaired, Cael reads the line as it is written without marking where he stands; Pike's "You're on my side." comes after the season line, and Cael then sees that he has read two leaves the right way up over the stump of an arm.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:728:- **The contract (44:165–215), as repaired.** Teague opens with the protected count and **closes** with "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more."; the four heads stand between in my words (neither healer on the count; shares and costs by the count; the field his; the reading Karis's). "The wall's still the wall." is **Teague's**, to Brom's "You've built your count on a thing that you've never seen stand."; Cael answers that there is a month on it with twelve days to run; Teague: "I'd not ask a thing with a month on it to be shown for a count." No hand is offered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:729:- **The meadow cart (44:219–265).** A salt cart sunk to its axle by the great ash; heel against the ash's root, palm on the cart's bed; every joint in one line, held three breaths; the cart goes the length of a body and stops dead; the wrist clicks at twenty strides; the young one's cloth. Brom names the Force and has seen one at a quarry. The protected line is **Teague's, said to the carter** who points at a second cart, in a voice that carries to the bench. Cael's log quotes none of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:739:- **The south road (45:193–243).** Vastin rides the salt cart to the fork above the mill on Teague's ruling and walks down the notch (ruled KEPT). After the protected log, one sentence marks what is Cael's own: only the ranking and a place older than two hundred and six are the paper's; "the centuries, and the figure near its foot, he had from a gallery" (45:231).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:740:- **Millrace (45:247–313), as repaired.** The woman with the net and Oryn's "I know." (KEPT). "Stand there." is Oryn's; Vastin hangs no clause on it; "Nineteen days," **Vastin**; "Then it's eleven more." **Oryn**. Teague speaks to Oryn for the first time; her answer in my words (three holds owed yet on this round, lying their way "for a day and some"; "You'll not count me, and you'll not send me. A crew doesn't write a well on its sheet because the road happens to pass it.") and then the protected "I'm a stop on my own route." A mark's worth of meal and a flitch: **127**. Brom sets her bowl before an upturned keg; "Sixth chair," **Lira**; "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **Oryn**; she sits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:741:- **The readings (45:317–409), as repaired.** Brom: the older healer unties her own knot; Oryn shuts the wrench in the left shoulder (the arm to the height of his chin); the right is re-tied in two yards; "That'll do." Lira: the protected three lines are Oryn / Lira / Oryn; "It's an arm." Karis: the seven stitches drawn; "Write. Don't lean." Vastin: he has stood at the post the better part of an hour; he tells her of the wall himself; "It held in a cut," **Oryn**, "And then you asked it for a second, with eleven days on it"; the slat off, two new laths, the month as counted; "Noted," **Vastin** / "That's new." **Oryn** / "It's a useful word." **Vastin** / "It's his." **Oryn**, who does not look round at the boy, and whose mouth goes down at one corner.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:749:### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:756:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Twelve fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He was a lamp for ten days and has entered it. He did not look back at the crown from the bridge. He has told Oryn the two self-readings of the 281st, the eleventh and the twelfth. He has told nobody the two words (*still*; *set*), the warning, or the date. He holds Oryn's finding word for word and has not written it; he has written that one thing came under her hands, unasked, and four reasons for not writing what. He has told Lira that something came and that he has no name for it. He walks at Teague's left and has said aloud that the field is Teague's. He lent the dividers twice and did not open them. *He has marked, beside the protected log, which of its claims are the paper's and which are his own.* The eleventh's debt stands. Body: sound; the eyes paid on the night of the 298th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:784:### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
