editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:800:## AFTER MOVEMENT 8 — chapters 47–53, days 299–305 (drafted 2026-10-12, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:802:### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:806:- **The crest (the 303rd, dusk).** The fourth place: a fence of iron bars a pace apart round a bowl; in the middle a grey arch on two piers over a sink — the carters' name, from Teague, is **the Sunken Span**. On a shelf between a dry ravine and the iron: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, two squared timbers on trestles, **seven hoods (two crossbows, four staves, one low practitioner who shows a white light)**. Protected: "They knew." (Karis); "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." (Seln); "Drawn?" (Teague); "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" (Cael) / **Teague's FIRST "Noted."** Vastin entered beforehand that he will not stand a wall (twenty-four of thirty).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:808:- **THE SPAN FIGHT (the 304th, first light).** (1) The watch called "Stand where you are, and declare"; nobody answered. Brom walked the shelf with Iron Skin up, silent, and took two bolts (breastbone; left forearm). (2) Teague went up the middle at a walk with **Cael at his left a stride back**, keeping his left side with the alley's cut stave for three breaths (a stave's shoe on Cael's left collar-bone; he did not give the stride). Teague put the barricade a body's length; the recoil went to the wrist **and then the elbow**. Protected: "Through." (Teague). **THE THIRTEENTH: Force-adjacent, from Teague, acquired at a stride** — protected, Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics: "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact … Deployment: none. Thirteenth." It does not ask; it **listens**. **Teague is not told.** (3) The watch reformed with one bow. Teague asked Karis whether the ground past the iron would bear a body ("It is ground."). Protected: Cael's entry before the act, "Nothing was gained inside."; then Teague handed him the ground past the iron ("You've stood on three of them. I've stood on none. Say how.") and Cael gave the order: "By count." **Five went over stake thirty-four: Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one ("Four."), Vastin** ("I am forbidden a wall. I am not, I think, forbidden to stand."); four stayed on the shelf (Teague, the tall man, Brom, the broad man with the second bow). Every ordinary Path went at the stride and came back whole at the stride ("It is all there … To the grain," Vastin); a place of twice the measure does as the three did. The five walked sixty strides inside the iron to the gap and stood: **eleven seconds**. "You'll die in there." (one of the watch) / "We've been in three times." (Cael). Cael refused the eleventh at the gap and the thirteenth at the ravine's lip. (4) **At the fourth second the watch's bow shot at the broad man's; he went over the ravine's lip with a yard of rotten shale, and Teague did not turn.** The seven went east through the gap one at a time and were not followed. **Win sentence (protected):** "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." **Nobody died. Nothing was opened inside the line.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:810:- **Costs.** **The broad man: the RIGHT shin (his good leg) broken clean;** laid straight by the older healer on her board and **knit by Oryn, asked first and answered in a word** (a quarter of an hour; she was grey; the two healers nodded to one another); he walks on a stick cut from the watch's trestle. **Teague's right arm: in linen to the shoulder on a slat, the hand not shutting** — protected: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." (Oryn) / "Noted," (Teague) / "Everybody says that now," (Oryn). Brom: two bruises, "a week of colours"; he carries the broad man's pack. Cael: a welt on the left collar-bone (ten days). The young one held his ground inside the line when the broad man fell, by watching Lira's boots.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:812:- **The Span itself (the 304th, noon).** Six went down (Karis, Lira, Brom, Seln, Vastin, Cael); Oryn tried Brom at the iron first ("Four … The same.") and would not be told a count across it. The arch is of the grey, in one piece with its piers, a cart's width, **no step**: a road on its back, never wheeled. **Cael stood on the crown: nothing.** The thirteenth listened to the grey; the old three ribs ached low on the left — the cost will come out of him there. Lira found the **square notch** in the hills on the line. Under the arch the sink goes down without a bottom; the piers' inner faces are cut in the floors' hand, and **Karis can read it**: nine sheets drawn. Protected: "Through" (Karis, of a word on the west pier). **Cael counted a course of fifty-two signs as fifty-one, twice** (ruling: hold). The twelfth took one unbidden breath of that course: *Goes.* **The log of the 304th (protected, whole, once):** "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth … Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like." (He let "tomorrow" stand: three days by the office's figure.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:815:- **THE LAMPS FINDING** (protected, Karis's, aloud, from her table of every crossing by seven people): "They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent." Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" (stopped). Karis: "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." **Two pages:** she tore the ruled leaf out and laid it at the corner farthest from the folded copy, with the whole blanket between and nothing across. **Vastin's THIRD "Noted."** **Cael did not add his own third page** (the technician's sheet stays at the foot of the second row; its day unsaid, unwritten; only he and Seln have done that sum).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:816:- **The two slips**, pinned under the knot of the oldest row's tape (protected): "*Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat.*" (red wax) / "*Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat.*" (dark wax, a different seal). Vastin: "Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack." / "The Compact," … "Yes. Part of it." (both Vastin's). **He knows both seals and names neither**; the slips are re-pinned where they were; nobody pried.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:821:- **The close of the 305th (protected, whole):** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." … "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." / "He was right. He did not yet know how right." **"Four hundred years" and "the Architect" stand nowhere else in the movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:824:### Review record
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:825:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial 295k; cold 118k; source-distance 200k (1 tracked passage; probe 2% / 9%); plan / canon / protected-text audit 630k tokens (REPAIR, bounded; forty-one exact fixes). **Fourteen applied by the coordinator** (the ten marker restorations, minimal, with the source's speakers; Lira's false memory of the plank; Karis's bar; two "five years"). **Twenty-seven DECLINED:** the read at the seep removed and deployment forced to thirty-two (no plan text fixes the figure); Karis's night stripped of the two pages (it is the plan's refusal); the year mechanism replaced by flat lines (the protected close needs its ground — the author trims the display instead); the gloss after the log; nested asterisks in the log; Seln's "one to a year"; a sentence telling Oryn of the thirteenth. **Repair r1 by the same author (claude-opus-5-5): the joins written, the year's display trimmed, the lean chain broken, listener anchors added; Sol recheck CLOSE with no line fixes.**
