    20	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
