    22	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 7 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 127 marks** at dawn on the 299th (130 less two for the rope, less one for meal at the mill; the rope debt to the Lowmarch ferryman is paid). Force was SEEN on the 298th (Teague, at a sunk salt cart: heel to palm in one line, a body's length, the recoil down the same line to the wrist) and **not acquired**; "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." is Teague's. (2) **The contract** (all Teague's words: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall."): the ten are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow (a broad man with a bad hip), the young one. **Neither healer is on it.** Shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's**; the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall is under a healer's month and is not stood before the month is out. **Teague's four know:** a survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; the four ages and "three days past the iron"; that an old man's wall stood in a cut. **They do NOT know** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf or the list, the date, or who Vastin was. The tall man, the bow and the older healer (a lean old woman with a staff and a board) have not yet spoken to the six. Teague has not yet said "Noted". (3) **March order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with **Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one, watching her feet; Karis, the two healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Four hand-signs, Lira's: flat hand *stand*; fist *seen*; two fingers *come on*; hand turned over empty *nothing*. (4) **Vastin: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; **he walks in the file from the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
