    24	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 8 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Thirteen fragments; deployment since the Line THIRTY-THREE; purse 123 marks** on the night of the 305th. The thirty-third use was the read on the wet ledge at the seep (the 302nd). The thirteenth is **Force-adjacent, from Teague**, acquired at a stride at the Span's timbers (the 304th); its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 8 and never reprinted. It does not ask; it **listens**. It has been lined dry once (the 305th: heel to a rib of rock, palm to a slab, every joint in one straight road) and **never let go**: "A trial; not counted." **Its first use belongs to this movement's pass** (on the second stack's brace, along the shelf; never at a person), and the cost comes back along the line to the place where the line leaves him — **the old three ribs, low on the left**. That use is a deployment and is counted. (2) **Who knows the thirteenth:** Cael; Lira; Brom; Karis and Seln by the log. **NOT Teague** (whose it was) **and NOT Vastin** (who also does not know the eleventh, his own): two unpaid debts, entered side by side, which cannot be paid without telling what is six people's. **Oryn has NOT been told** — she refused the count across the iron on the 304th, and Cael means to tell her "when she'll hear it"; "Ribs. May I?" … "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." is where she meets it. Teague thanked Cael for keeping his left at the timbers and does not know what Cael came away with. (3) **Teague's right arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand does not shut**; Oryn: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint." He goes up the pass's stair LEFT-handed. **The tall man's spear is HIS** (he / him; this packet's "reverses her spear" is the source's pronoun and is overridden — OWNER #59). The tall man and the older healer have still not spoken to the six; the broad man's first word to them was "Aye" on the 305th. **The broad man:** right shin (his good leg) broken at the Span, knit by Oryn, boarded, walking on a stick cut from the watch's trestle, at the tail; his crossbow's stock is split by a bolt. **The young one** went over the iron when Teague looked at him ("Four."), held his feet inside the line by watching Lira's boots, "goes wherever he is looked at, a half-beat before he has seen what is there", and nods with his whole head; he is still unnamed (OWNER-pending #54 governs the one saying of his name). (4) **What Teague's four know:** five people stood whole inside the line; a boy kept a captain's left with a stick; nothing of the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf, the lamps page, the slips, the date, or who Vastin was. **The doctrine "behind it" has NOT been told to them; no wall has been drilled or stood.** Vastin entered on the 303rd that he will not stand a wall before his month is out (he stood inside the line at the Span instead, and what he carries went and came back "to the grain"); the 306th is **day twenty-seven of thirty**. (5) **The watch** (seven, hooded, faceless: two crossbows, four staves, one low practitioner) went east through the gap a day ahead, carrying one broken bow; they saw silent Iron take bolts, silent Force shift timber, and five people stand inside the line; they saw nothing work inside. Nobody died at the Span. **Seln** looked at the square notch from a mile on the evening of the 305th: a dry bed going in, the only way through for five miles either hand, no fire, nobody on either wall, not a heel-mark — "I looked at it." — and is to look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves. (6) **Pages, and who holds each:** Karis has the torn ruled leaf with the lamps finding ("They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent.") in the back of her notebook, and under her initial "*Second page: nothing entered. Not for want of a pencil.*"; Cael has the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book; the technician's sheet lies at the foot of the second row in the flat, its day unsaid and unwritten (only Cael and Seln have done that sum, each alone). **Nobody has laid one of these across another; Cael added no page of his own; Vastin's sentence stopped twice.** The two sealed slips are re-pinned under the knot of the oldest row; Vastin knows both seals and has named neither ("That's a crack." … "The Compact," … "Yes. Part of it."). (7) **The fifth place:** a thumbnail ring round the divider's prick on the clean sheet, uninked until corded; "three days past the iron, a little less" (one walked on the 305th); its two corner signs are a year written by its first letters in the old town's count, which Karis worked alone and said once, in the close of the 305th: "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." **In this movement "four hundred years" may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it; "the Architect" not at all unless the plan prints it.** Every row on every sheet leans the one way, along the brass, east (one unbidden glance of the twelfth, entered by Karis as Cael's and unchecked). At the Span a course of fifty-two signs counted as fifty-one in Cael's hands, twice (ruling: hold) — the instruments' trend. (8) **Oryn** is five days past her cairn on the 305th (the cairn is at noon on the 300th; six on the 306th, seven on the 307th, eight on the 308th); three holds still owe her a visit and have had word ("a week, or more"). She has not heard the leaf. She knit a shin on the 304th (asked first, answered in a word) and had her hands in it again on the 305th under the older healer's binding. **Nobody has yet died under her hands.** (9) **Bodies otherwise:** Brom, two bruises in "a week of colours", both arms sound to the shoulder, carrying the broad man's pack; Cael, a welt on the left collar-bone and the ribs speaking; Karis, the left palm in linen ("Write. Don't lean."); Lira, the arm whole. **Load:** the mule has the three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas; Vastin the tarred case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two, never driven); Cael Hesk's book with the dividers shut in it (opened only ever by Karis). (10) **Seln's case is "shut"**, on his chest, contents unnamed, no count of years.
