   865	**Calendar.** The night of the **three hundred and fifth day past the Line**, on a shelf of shale under a step, four or five miles short of a square gap in the hills to the east, a day's walk past the fourth place. Days on the page: 299 (the ridge; the Stair's brow; the beck), 300 (the cairn at noon; the track; the hall's marsh at dusk), 301 (the east road; the dead hold), 302 (the chock-stones; the ridge; the seep; the hollow), 303 (the ridge; the brow at dusk; the fold; Seln's night), 304 (the shelf at first light; the ravine's bed; the hut; the Span at noon; the watch's fire at dusk), 305 (round the fence; the shale; the blanket; one fire; the step; Karis's lamp; Seln's return). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
   866	
   867	**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule in one camp under the step, at one fire in two halves: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man, the broad man, the young one, the older healer; Oryn and the brown mule. Seln is back from the gap and is to look again at first light; nobody moves until he has. Cleon is under Treswick. Pike is at Lowmarch. The watch's seven went east along the perimeter path on the morning of the 304th and have not been seen since.
