   874	
   875	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck. She has: the cord's figure at the Stair confirmed; nine sheets of the piers' inner faces; one word turned on the west pier ("Through"); the agreement of fourteen sheets' rows with the brass, and which way, entered as Cael's and unchecked (she has refused "the next"); the two corner signs read as an old-style year, which her night's reduction shows to be near the skin's year and does not show to be the same; the point ringed with a thumbnail; **the lamps finding**, said aloud and filed on a leaf torn from her notebook, which is now in the back of that notebook with the line "Second page: nothing entered. Not for want of a pencil."; the two slips entered as present, under two unlike seals, unnamed. She has said the figure once, to Cael, at the close. She said "They knew" on the brow. She knows that a six-word sentence exists and has not said or written it. She still has not said the office's compass point or its figure in lengths aloud. Left palm in linen; she writes; she carried a box one-handed.
   876	
   877	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He read three ages of iron in the fence and the watch's habits from the grass; counted seven out; looked at the gap from a mile and saw nothing, and does not like it. He has seen a keg's hoop and five made heels at the seep. He gave the watchman's stave to Cael. The case is on his breastbone, shut; nothing about it is altered; not mentioned aloud.
