    10	
    11	The tall man had been gathering all that while. He had brought flat stones up out of the bed, one at a time, and set them edge to edge upon the rock in a shape as long as a person. He lifted the blanket onto it by himself. Cael had not known until then how slight a boy could be who was all wrists and collar.
    12	
    13	Then the broad man came, on his stick.
    14	
