    95	## Guards
    96	
    97	- The young one is never named and no sound of his name is rendered; nobody in Teague's crew is named.
    98	- No possessive before "Path" in narration. No season, month or weekday name. Feet, yards, miles, paces, strides, cords. No count of years since the Kindling; nineteen; no age for Vastin.
    99	- *Still* / *set* and what follows them: told to nobody. The leaf: quoted by nobody; Oryn has not heard it. No line from the leaf to the lamps finding in any mouth or head. Never *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; never *recurrence*, *primordial*, *source*, *tomb*; "the court" lowercase. "Four hundred years" only inside the closing prose. "The Architect" nowhere.
   100	- The site does nothing and wants nothing; no maker's present will; the instruments' trend has no cause given. The third sentence is nowhere but in the closing prose's own words.
   101	- Every reading has consent on the page; where it cannot be asked, the page says so.
   102	- Vastin does not ask and is not asked; no vote; nothing of what comes after. Teague is not told. Seln's case is "shut", on his chest, contents unnamed, no count of years.
   103	- No cutaway at the court by Oryn.
