   109	- **Chapter boundaries.** 54 ends with the roof up and the second flight on it; 55 holds flights three to seven, the push, the breaking, the release and the far mouth; 56 the burial, Seln's two scenes, the bowls and the ribs; 57 Oryn's two scenes, the instruments, the inward turn and the log; 58 the plain, the round, the cuts, the council and the line, ending on the S23 marker; 59 the centre, the line again and Vastin's two scenes; 60 the ledger, the letter, the two departures and the close.
   110	- **Decision 7.** Brom is in the middle with Oryn (having the bolt's feathers broken off, asked first) when the broad man goes to the high edge; he walks out into the open end only before the seventh flight.
   111	- **Decision 9–10 (timing).** Cael does not keep the captain's shoulder on the run. A heavy man with one arm lashed goes at a hard jog over loose stone and the tall man will not leave him; Cael outruns them, is under the second heap at the count of eight and at the lip at twenty, with the two of them under it as the frame begins to lean. Teague's distance from the roof's edge to the heap is "five and thirty strides". Seln calls the count ("Nine.") down from the lip, raising his voice for the first time.
   112	- **Decision 11.** To reach the cleft the nine pass within a pole's length of Teague and the tall man, and the three bowmen pass the boy on his knees; nobody lifts a hand on either side. The tall man grounds the butt once when the last is by (his yard-sign for a touch taken).
   113	- **Decision 14.** Vastin is got to his feet by Karis for the burial against what a healer said he had in him; he cannot lift a bowl that night (Lira feeds him).
   114	- **Decision 16.** The ribs are read away from the fire, round a shoulder of the rock, so that neither an old man nor a captain's three can overhear whose line it is. Oryn's two scenes and the inward turn happen at that same place.
   115	- **Decision 18.** The instruments are tried after dark, by Karis's lamp, with Karis and **Brom** (not Lira) laying the measure first.
   116	- **Decision 24.** Karis's evidence for the first cut is a slip of the cutter's tool at the corner of one sign, which stands, cut on purpose and at full depth, on her sheets from the west pier and from the hall.
   117	- **Decision 25.** The team's marks go **south** from the foot of their path (not north), which leaves Oryn's road north clear.
   118	- **Decision 27.** On the walk in he thinks of the plate; the last four hundred and six strides are walked half blind toward the lowest smear of light in the east. Walking back he steers by the crews' fire.
   119	- **Decision 30–31.** Added in chapter 60: Seln's one remark at the ledger (three reaches; he does not think the third the last); the tall man's second night with the cloth; the broad man's "Aye" to Vastin at parting; the tall man's grounded butt to Cael; Lira's hand on his sleeve in the night. The closing prose is led in by one paragraph of mine that sets it on the walk back of the night before, so that its "now, walking back out" is true where it stands.
   120	- **Protected units.** "Ribs. May I?" was first drafted split across two speeches and is now one line. A second "It's mine now" in Oryn's head, a second "Sixth chair" and a second "By count" were written and taken out again, so that each stands once.

