editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:16:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:20:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:22:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 7 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 127 marks** at dawn on the 299th (130 less two for the rope, less one for meal at the mill; the rope debt to the Lowmarch ferryman is paid). Force was SEEN on the 298th (Teague, at a sunk salt cart: heel to palm in one line, a body's length, the recoil down the same line to the wrist) and **not acquired**; "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." is Teague's. (2) **The contract** (all Teague's words: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall."): the ten are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow (a broad man with a bad hip), the young one. **Neither healer is on it.** Shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's**; the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall is under a healer's month and is not stood before the month is out. **Teague's four know:** a survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; the four ages and "three days past the iron"; that an old man's wall stood in a cut. **They do NOT know** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf or the list, the date, or who Vastin was. The tall man, the bow and the older healer (a lean old woman with a staff and a board) have not yet spoken to the six. Teague has not yet said "Noted". (3) **March order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with **Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one, watching her feet; Karis, the two healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Four hand-signs, Lira's: flat hand *stand*; fist *seen*; two fingers *come on*; hand turned over empty *nothing*. (4) **Vastin: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; **he walks in the file from the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:24:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 8 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Thirteen fragments; deployment since the Line THIRTY-THREE; purse 123 marks** on the night of the 305th. The thirty-third use was the read on the wet ledge at the seep (the 302nd). The thirteenth is **Force-adjacent, from Teague**, acquired at a stride at the Span's timbers (the 304th); its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 8 and never reprinted. It does not ask; it **listens**. It has been lined dry once (the 305th: heel to a rib of rock, palm to a slab, every joint in one straight road) and **never let go**: "A trial; not counted." **Its first use belongs to this movement's pass** (on the second stack's brace, along the shelf; never at a person), and the cost comes back along the line to the place where the line leaves him — **the old three ribs, low on the left**. That use is a deployment and is counted. (2) **Who knows the thirteenth:** Cael; Lira; Brom; Karis and Seln by the log. **NOT Teague** (whose it was) **and NOT Vastin** (who also does not know the eleventh, his own): two unpaid debts, entered side by side, which cannot be paid without telling what is six people's. **Oryn has NOT been told** — she refused the count across the iron on the 304th, and Cael means to tell her "when she'll hear it"; "Ribs. May I?" … "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." is where she meets it. Teague thanked Cael for keeping his left at the timbers and does not know what Cael came away with. (3) **Teague's right arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand does not shut**; Oryn: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint." He goes up the pass's stair LEFT-handed. **The tall man's spear is HIS** (he / him; this packet's "reverses her spear" is the source's pronoun and is overridden — OWNER #59). The tall man and the older healer have still not spoken to the six; the broad man's first word to them was "Aye" on the 305th. **The broad man:** right shin (his good leg) broken at the Span, knit by Oryn, boarded, walking on a stick cut from the watch's trestle, at the tail; his crossbow's stock is split by a bolt. **The young one** went over the iron when Teague looked at him ("Four."), held his feet inside the line by watching Lira's boots, "goes wherever he is looked at, a half-beat before he has seen what is there", and nods with his whole head; he is still unnamed (OWNER-pending #54 governs the one saying of his name). (4) **What Teague's four know:** five people stood whole inside the line; a boy kept a captain's left with a stick; nothing of the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf, the lamps page, the slips, the date, or who Vastin was. **The doctrine "behind it" has NOT been told to them; no wall has been drilled or stood.** Vastin entered on the 303rd that he will not stand a wall before his month is out (he stood inside the line at the Span instead, and what he carries went and came back "to the grain"); the 306th is **day twenty-seven of thirty**. (5) **The watch** (seven, hooded, faceless: two crossbows, four staves, one low practitioner) went east through the gap a day ahead, carrying one broken bow; they saw silent Iron take bolts, silent Force shift timber, and five people stand inside the line; they saw nothing work inside. Nobody died at the Span. **Seln** looked at the square notch from a mile on the evening of the 305th: a dry bed going in, the only way through for five miles either hand, no fire, nobody on either wall, not a heel-mark — "I looked at it." — and is to look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves. (6) **Pages, and who holds each:** Karis has the torn ruled leaf with the lamps finding ("They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent.") in the back of her notebook, and under her initial "*Second page: nothing entered. Not for want of a pencil.*"; Cael has the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book; the technician's sheet lies at the foot of the second row in the flat, its day unsaid and unwritten (only Cael and Seln have done that sum, each alone). **Nobody has laid one of these across another; Cael added no page of his own; Vastin's sentence stopped twice.** The two sealed slips are re-pinned under the knot of the oldest row; Vastin knows both seals and has named neither ("That's a crack." … "The Compact," … "Yes. Part of it."). (7) **The fifth place:** a thumbnail ring round the divider's prick on the clean sheet, uninked until corded; "three days past the iron, a little less" (one walked on the 305th); its two corner signs are a year written by its first letters in the old town's count, which Karis worked alone and said once, in the close of the 305th: "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." **In this movement "four hundred years" may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it; "the Architect" not at all unless the plan prints it.** Every row on every sheet leans the one way, along the brass, east (one unbidden glance of the twelfth, entered by Karis as Cael's and unchecked). At the Span a course of fifty-two signs counted as fifty-one in Cael's hands, twice (ruling: hold) — the instruments' trend. (8) **Oryn** is five days past her cairn on the 305th (the cairn is at noon on the 300th; six on the 306th, seven on the 307th, eight on the 308th); three holds still owe her a visit and have had word ("a week, or more"). She has not heard the leaf. She knit a shin on the 304th (asked first, answered in a word) and had her hands in it again on the 305th under the older healer's binding. **Nobody has yet died under her hands.** (9) **Bodies otherwise:** Brom, two bruises in "a week of colours", both arms sound to the shoulder, carrying the broad man's pack; Cael, a welt on the left collar-bone and the ribs speaking; Karis, the left palm in linen ("Write. Don't lean."); Lira, the arm whole. **Load:** the mule has the three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas; Vastin the tarred case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two, never driven); Cael Hesk's book with the dividers shut in it (opened only ever by Karis). (10) **Seln's case is "shut"**, on his chest, contents unnamed, no count of years.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:36:> - **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She does NOT yet know of the thirteenth or of what it would cost his ribs (coordinator ruling), and does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:38:> - **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:50:It is first light on the 306th, at the shale camp below the notch. Seln comes back wet to the ankle from the pass's floor. Twelve and a mule. Vastin is on day 27. The ribs have been quiet since the marsh, and the thirteenth is listening.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:66:- **Burial and the plain's edge (306th).** Teague's crew builds the cairn in their own order. The six carry at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." **"That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now."** No term tonight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:72:- **The ledger, the letter and the dawn (307th night–308th), verbatim.** Teague: "After the next thaw … My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Oryn: "The day I have to." … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] "Six. Six and no mule." Vastin is unadmitted. "West." **Closing prose, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:75:**Cutaways (~5,800):** Seln, ~1,800, on the ridge with Lira to recover the mule: the swept scree below, the dead pine. Oryn, ~2,000, the night after the first death under her hands. **She has not heard the leaf. No cutaway at the court.** Vastin, ~2,000, at the court's rim at night: the line he never asked about. **He is unadmitted and not asking. There is no hint of Book 9's request.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:94:West, six and no mule. Three holds still owe a healer a visit. A captain walks home past a cairn. A marshal with a stick has stood at the line where they drew it and has not asked. Thirteen fragments. A still place read by two instruments and understood by neither. A third sentence waits past *exclude* and *prevent* that he is not ready to write. Book 9 begins with that sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:25:- **Letters/animals:** Hesk's brass and note and Oryn's bark have arrived. Letters to Hesk and Vell went west on the last ferry; Ephram's is deferred to the first boat of the thaw. The brown mule is with the five. Oryn has the grey jenny and the thirty-foot three-strand rope. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:29:- **Pike/the Compact:** Pike has nine completed lines under the five names; the ninth is the Stair and reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The first-snow season line is written with no number against it. The five names remain **eleventh**. The Compact has a Fallow completion report, the Stair rim's observations and a clerk's packet saying the crew kept the kit; it does not know that fragments work inside. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4] It has reached across the Line twice: on paper (the Fallow completion report) and in person (the six on the Stair's rim). The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:40:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **Count at the rim:** "Six. Six and no mule." That is Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin. The word is "West."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:59:7. **KEEP — Six at Lowmarch (268th).** 118 marks (the mule's shed and the rope-house roof). Karis makes her case to six: the carvings are instructions; the index; west; **Treswick and the Deepstacks named**; the scholars' provision; "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **KEEP — the closing log (270th)**, verbatim (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:66:14. **KEEP — The fork-stone (280th evening–281st first light).** Oryn's terms: "I'm not an archive person"; the city she left; "Leaving and routing are different verbs." "Three weeks" (Seln). **The promise** is written in the log and read back. She prices everyone. The Millrace rendezvous. "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with her. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. Treswick comes into view from the rise; the light on the crown is not looked at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:68:16. **KEEP — Treswick's outer district (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts and does not ask. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of the crew looks in their own way. "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." "They shoe by the tier." The road to the registry crosses the square, and the promise holds. Seln's report: the quarry; the provision; hands by count, up to four; the clerk; the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." The close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:83:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:92:40. **KEEP — The ledger, the letter, and the dawn (307th night–308th).** Teague goes west carrying the letter; Oryn goes north; "Six. Six and no mule."; Vastin is unadmitted; "West." The closing prose (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:114:| **NEW — Water at the seep** (301st–302nd, dry camps) | "two camps with no water" | 3,000 | The two crews must water themselves and a mule at a seep where shale-backs stand on a slope. Teague's field captaincy is shown. The young one moves too fast and the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] stops him with a hand. That is his habit, set up for the pass. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:115:| **Lesser exchanges given their beats** | — | ~4,500 | The alley's aftermath; the Span's broad-man fall; the ridge recovery of the mule; the court's pacing as a physical task. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:136:- **The burial and the mule** (≈2,000).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:161:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:195:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:239:| 299 | Dawn: twelve and a mule; the Stair's bowl |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty-five yards below [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:394:- **S4 lesson and log:** "The wall held the line," … "And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." … "I have never once in forty years needed someone else to be the reason." / "You do now," / "I know fields. I don't know packs." … "I'll learn or I won't." Log: "Vastin fought. He rooted the road and nearly got eaten for it — a wall's no good if you're the only thing making noise behind it. He knows fields. He doesn't know packs. He'll learn or he won't. Watched an Iron Wall go up two feet from me. Filed it. Note the day: an Archmarshal took a wound out here and there was no one to report it to. He looked almost free. Almost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:470:- **The mule** goes north with Oryn on the 281st and returns at Millrace on the 298th. From the fork to Millrace the boxes are carried on backs (ruling 16).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:28:**Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:40:**Oryn knows:** the mechanism by Path, the full still-place telling and label, and the three entered sites on one bearing. She left at the day-122 fork and does not know the day-123 fourth-site survey or result at entry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:46:**The Compact knows:** quiet ground exists and stops Arbiters; the Fallow completion report identifies the crew; the Stair rim saw a declaration; a clerk's packet says the crew kept the kit. It does not know that Cael's fragments work inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:48:**He does not know:** that the index is a grade; the Architect; Treswick's archive or Cleon; anything Vastin carries; that instruments will read wrong in his hands. The last is discovered on the 168th (Book 7 ends with the instruments reading TRUE in his hand; Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:63:- **Animals/boxes:** brown mule with the five; grey jenny with Oryn. Three boxes at the back room's warm wall; reserve in the third.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:121:- **Seam with the locked Book 7 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 131 at Lowmarch; the five; ten fragments; the debt to Oryn paid, not forgiven; the still place told and here neither read nor touched; the fourth site unentered and untested; the kit, the dead man's ledger and fifty-two sheets; the brown mule with the five.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- **The stroke and bar** is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only. Karis cannot read the index and does not know it is a grade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:138:- **What four a month buys (flag):** the hearth's end; the pot at dusk, a bowl a head; and the crew's names said to anybody who comes asking. Not bread, candles, the back room or the mule. "A cold term's five by my book": twenty, in front. The keeper comes out to his own door, behind the plank, to hear his floor priced (the join for the restored `The keeper said, "Pike," and Pike said, "Eleventh."`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:147:- **The ice road (flag):** a four-wheeled cart behind two mules, eighty yards out, with a dozen barrels and two pigs of iron for the smith; the carter heavy and grey-bearded, unnamed; one barrel of fish lost. Hauled out on the ferry's own rope and drum by Oryn's brown mule. Pike: "That's said. It's not entered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:155:- **Thornwater's yard (repair r1):** the mule finds Oryn first; she is on her heels at the bench's end binding an old man's hand, and her right hand goes out behind her to the mule's cheek; she looks the five over only after the old man is sent off, Cael first and briefly, then Brom's knot, Lira's boot, and last the sling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:162:**Where everyone is.** Six at the lower inn: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, and Oryn, who came down from Thornwater unasked because Lowmarch is her first stop after a thaw and the mill her second. Her brown mule is in the ferryman's shed. The mill's grey jenny is not mentioned after Book 7. Teague's five are at the upper inn; they do not appear after the 190th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:174:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. She released the arm only when Lira took it; mended the ankle; answered Lira's thanks with "Route's whole… The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."; left the shoulder to the woman who tied it. She has seen the map with four rings and the line ("That's a line.") and has been told of the fourth site: twice the size, fenced, unentered. She has been told of the cord and the edges. **She has not read Cael** and has said that she will know what she is reading for before she does. At the word *station* she shut her mouth on a sentence and said nothing. She did not sit in the sixth place. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:180:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand** (96 − 20 for the cold stay; + 40 for the fence; + 5 for the roof; − 3 for the mule's shed). The reserve sealed and unopened. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, wanted with the first boat; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. Both brass edges are in their cloths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:200:- **Oryn:** she knows the fourth-site description, the map line, and the instrument anomaly, but has not read Cael and will not until she knows the purpose (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-209`). She did not take the sixth chair (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:223-225`). Her grey jenny remains at Thornwater; the brown mule is with the six at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:65-77,217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:202:- **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:216:- **Seln went still at the date** and said only "I have read it." He has not said the sum. Cael does not know what it was and has not read the date closely. **Nobody has connected the date to anyone**, and nobody has interpreted the sequence. "Classification event" is not defined.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:221:- **Lowmarch:** the mule's stool at the board's end (Oryn stands beside it); Pike's new cloth, Teague first, the five carried **eleventh** by place; Oryn's bench a yard past Pike's right-hand post; the first boat took people only; the hauling rope has two yarns gone and the stern strap is improvised; the sixty yards of cordage are still on the western bank and the rope debt stands; the hurdle is paid. Ephram's letter went west on the afternoon boat. **Purse: 118 marks.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:232:- **The mule's stool (flag):** a three-legged milking stool from the keeper's kitchen, set at the board's end on the 271st with the sixth bowl. Oryn will not sit on it; Lira names it; Vastin asks whether the place is taken and is told whose it is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:241:- **The completion report (repaired to Book 7).** It carries the Fallow posting's head, a town on no registry map and a board; **"where a crew's name should have been there were five strokes, and after the strokes a count, which was six."** No names. It reached Vastin as a courtesy copy with no routing note; it took him the cold term to find the file that it belonged to, "which stands in no register". He does not know who had the abstracts held, and looked. Whether the copy was sent to him on purpose is Seln's question, left open.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:244:- **The sheet (repaired):** thin stock, newer than the rest, a printed head, "a quick sloping hand"; a technician's return ("When a man who services the stations finds a thing that he was not sent to find, he is bound to write it up on such a sheet, on the day, and send it in"). **The office had filed it with the surveys, at the end of the second row; Vastin carried it in the lid to keep it dry; Karis has laid it back at the foot of the second row.** Its date is a registry year and a day in it, in the office's reckoning; **no figures are printed anywhere.** The bar is as broad as a thumb, laid on both sides, cracked in drying; Vastin has seen such a bar "on perhaps a dozen papers in forty years" and never with initials. He does not know which classification event is meant.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:252:**Where everyone is.** Seven under the lower inn's roof: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln; Oryn, who is on her road and at her bench by first light; and **Vastin, in the loft over the tap, at a copper a night**, who is on nobody's sheet and has asked for nothing but a bed. Teague's five are at the upper inn, with forty sacks of salt on the bank. The brown mule is in the ferryman's shed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:264:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. A bench under the eave since the 272nd. She saw the bout and said nothing. She has not asked about the knee, and Vastin has offered it to nobody; she seconded Karis's order to bed with one line about the stairs. **She has not read Cael.** She has shut her mouth three times on the same sentence. She did not sit on the stool. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:266:**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named.** He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt in his coat. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"), on the authority of the office's own page; that the one line which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive (his own copy of it); that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, which classification event the sheet means, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He was sent to bed, began to argue twice, took four stairs fast and the rest slowly; whether that was the order or the knee is not settled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:286:- **What each knows.** All six and Vastin have heard no key, the citation/title/place, suppressed survey records and the technician's visible line/bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:149–193`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:59–151`). Karis has not finished the records and cannot read the index or bar (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:129–135,285–289`). Seln has done an unexplained sum and said only “I have read it”; Cael does not know the sum (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Vastin does not know the integration mechanism, directive, objection, what Cael carries, or what lies under the bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:119–129`). Nobody connects the date to anyone (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Oryn has not read Cael and has not asked to read Vastin's knee (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:29–47`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:306:- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:320:- **The ferry and the rope.** On the 278th she crossed in the forenoon with people, led beasts and carried sacks; no wheels. A copper a head, the mule a head. **The broker's cordage on the western landing is three-strand, hawser-laid. Brom refused it.** The sixty yards of four-strand are still owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:324:- **The shoulder hold and its factor.** A foot-track from a cairn below the spur; a plain bar in a wall as thick as a cart; a small clean yard, a long low house, a salting-shed with empty hooks. The factor: spare, grey, a leather apron, a slate on a cord, a sheep-crook, pale eyes; a thumb-mark like a crook; **no name and no pronoun on the page**. Three carts, a carter and two mules lost since the frost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:347:**Where everyone is.** Six going down off the rise: Seln in front, Lira, Brom, Karis, and then **Cael with Vastin walking beside him on the ditch side** (from the top of the rise; nobody asked him to and nobody told him no). Oryn and the brown mule went north from the fork at first light and did not look back. Teague's five are east of the river.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:357:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. One hound with a short knife; "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe". **He has read the original date in daylight, has told nobody, and has set the sheet before Cael without a word; he does not know for certain that it was read.** He has taught for the first time ("Draft nothing. Just look.", to Vastin). **He carries no box.** **The case is on him, shut; no ruling upon it.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:359:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. On Pike's slip as its healer. She asked Vastin and had an explicit yes; shut four holes; bound the joint; two fingers on his wrist. She has priced all six and given Vastin as long as any. **She has not read Cael**: "It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." She has told the house, the column and why she left, and will not say where. She has her term in his log and has read it there. Gone north with the mule, her linen, and her crossbow with its one bolt; five gates, the ford, then Millrace in three weeks. She does not know that Vastin is carrying the kit's case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:361:**Vastin.** No office; **no age stated**. **Iron Wall declared once, on the 279th, in the cut**; spent to the floor. **Right knee: bitten, shut, bound stiff; the 281st is the second day of thirty**; on the stick; no kneeling, running or walls. He qualified every instruction. **He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut.** **He carries the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two) on the shoulder above his sound leg, taken up unasked at the fork-stone after Oryn had gone, and has told Cael so.** **He walks beside Cael from the top of the rise.** He said the town's name at the spring, the first to say it since the page. He knows the four hands, the doctrine and where a post stands. He has heard the daylight reading whole. **He does not know that the date means anything to anybody**, the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, or what is under the bar; nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:378:Movement 4 already carries day 281, six people/no mule, boxes on Brom/Lira/Cael, kit case on Vastin, the road posts, the inward reads, the station promise, and no new fragment (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,31–33,43–46`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving details:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:381:- **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:383:- **Oryn:** she and the brown mule are north of the fork on the reverse circuit; she has her linen and crossbow with one bolt. Her stated route is five gates, the ford and Millrace, where she expects the six in three weeks; she still owes Cael the proper reading and expects “all of it” from the archive (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:63–81,171–219`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:394:- **Entry seam with Movement 3 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 281 going down off the rise; six and no mule; the loads; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; purse 138; bodies; the papers with Karis (the flat, the hide, the copied page in oilcloth, the dead surveyor's ledger, her notebook).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:420:- **The outer district.** The brokers' street from the gate to the bluff's foot, with a slate tally board at every door (*Wanted*; a load or a number of hands; the landing, the second wall or the third; a rate; a daub of colour for the card that goes with the work); the porters' bench; loads up on the right hand and down on the left. The rope-walk: a shed three hundred yards long against the inside of the town wall, ending in a yard of tar barrels above a quay; **Brom found four-strand laid round a heart, asked the price of sixty yards, found it fair, and did not buy** ("I'll take it going out"); no figure is printed. A public trough forty feet long at the street's head, where a brown mule that is not theirs was drinking (theirs has the white foot). A ring road under the second wall, right round the bluff. A landing with six flat boats, a treadwheel hoist and a cable ferry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:429:- **Vastin.** He told Cael beforehand that he would sit and could not rise without him; he sat on the bank at the three-mile post (the first time since the cut), in the inn's lower room (the second), and on the yard's bench (the third). **What he says of the file:** he read it first in the week before he came up the bluff, by the candles of four inns, and last on the morning he left a seal in a tray. **Why he declined (as repaired, in line with locked Book 6):** the reason he gave at Ostrand *was* the reason and he does not take it back: five young people had shown him what the office he served did with honest readings, and he would not lend it his name for one more; he wrote *declined* on a form that has no line for why, and would have written it had there been no night awake. **What he adds, and has told nobody else:** he had set out what a second reading could come to (a second silence, for which an office finds a word; or a plate that lit, which would have made his three days and nine thousand readings worth what a sheet of brass said); he could afford neither answer; it was the second that kept him awake; and when the pen was down he was relieved, on his own account, that he need never learn what the plate would say. "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one." He answers for the refusal and takes no credit for the gladness. His sentence from forty years of inquiries, "The instrument is not at fault. It has told you where its reach ends," is said aloud here; he wrote it once of a person, in an assessment that a seat declined to receive (Book 6). **His papers:** three sheets under one seal, in oilskin, which would open both gates and bring an officer down the hill; he does not know who reads the town's books at night. He has certified the town four times. In his window: every district he inspected had been told four days before that he was coming.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:439:**Where everyone is.** Five inside the iron door: Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin, Cael, with Cleon at the stair's head holding one lamp. The clerk is outside it with his lantern. **Seln is above ground, on no card, where he can see who comes to look at the door**; nobody saw him on the climb. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second of her five gates, north along the hill-foot, with three gates, the ford and Millrace ahead and her day in hand spent. Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:447:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; shut since the fork. She has said, on the evidence of her own eyes, that the bridge is older than the walls; she has seen the same dark stone under the registry's back and under her bare hand in the undercroft, and has said nothing of it yet. She laid one sheet on a counter, answered a craftsman's questions, and **said that she came to ask how the thing stands, not what it says**. She has agreed to his terms and has kept her case to herself. She carried the card as its bearer; it has two corners gone. She holds the flat, the hide, the page in her coat, the ledger and her notebook. She has told Cael that she cannot tell her happiness from terror. She does not know what Cael meant by "look up" and did not ask.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:451:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: the fifth day of thirty on the 284th**; on the stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall. It did nine miles on the 281st and twenty-two steps down on the 284th; the stick slipped once and he caught himself on the wall with the left hand. **He has sat three times.** He has told Cael the rest of why he declined the second reading: the Ostrand reason stands as the cause, and beside it his private relief at never learning what a plate would say (glad of a right act for a wrong reason). He holds what Cael gave him and has not asked what read it. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does no date arithmetic. He has said once that he has papers he will not show. He consented to be the fourth before he was asked and went through three counts as a hand, looking at his boots, "very ill" and then a little better; the clerk looked at him after the line was blotted, opened his mouth, and did not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He carries the kit case, still against the letter of Oryn's instruction; Oryn does not know.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:453:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. Two gates done of five. She parted and re-knit a carter's wrist at the first (asked; told yes in the morning) and turned a child at the second (asked; told yes). **Nobody has died under her hands.** She is spent to grey and a day behind her own reckoning. She has not been through a gate. She has the mule, her linen and the crossbow. She owes Cael the reading and has thought about it twice; she has heard of no leaf and knows nothing of what happened on the road's edge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:468:- **Who is below.** Inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with Cleon at the stair head; the unnamed clerk and his lantern remain outside. Seln is above ground, not on the 284th card or count, positioned to see who comes to the door. Oryn and the brown mule are at the second unnamed gate north (`ch25:87–117`; `ch26:183–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:101`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:518:- **Brom's yard.** A broker's dray (two wheels as tall as Lira, one mule, a square of slate painted on its side) loaded with roofing slate shed its near wheel on the yard's slope; the slates slid and pinned the carter's lad by the boot against the dock's kerb. Brom stopped the yard-men's lever at the high side, took the low corner on his left shoulder with no grey, held while Lira drew the lad out by his belt, and was let down onto two split logs driven under the axle by Cael and a yard-man. The lad's five toes bend. **The broker's factor** (a good grey cloak, a broad hat, a shaved chin, clean hands, a tally; no name, no face): the house is the third on the brokers' street with the slate above its door; a guard's post at its store inside the second wall; a standing pass, sealed, by the month; a bed in the house above the wall; the house's coat; **four marks, and found**. His master "keeps eleven on his doors" who will not shift a keg until they have lit up, "and then it's a line in somebody's book". Brom: "I'd have taken it at sixteen and written home the same night."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:521:- **Vastin.** At the yard on the 286th he held the dray's mule by the cheek-strap with the left hand and gave no order. On the 287th he moved toward the lamp four times (Lira counted); on the 288th twice; on the 290th not at all. On the 288th he began to post a watch and stopped ("That's one"). On the 289th he held three tall books at Lira's word, qualifying it ("I cannot undertake to carry them to a table"). His three heads on the night of the 290th: the knee (he had Oryn's words in his mind as the stick came down, and asks that she be told that he heard her); what the six came for (they looked past him at Cael); and that he knows no more of what Cael is than the plate did.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:532:**Where everyone is.** Six in the loft: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Vastin (on a pallet under the blanketed gable window, unable to stand), and Seln on the ladder's head. Cleon is under the registry with fifty-two sheets on three tables, the board against the third, and tomorrow's card written and given. The clerk has written *the same* on six days. Oryn and the brown mule are north on her round (not on the page in this movement). Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:544:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **He stood a wall on the eleventh day of thirty.** The knee let go sideways when he released it; one lath cracked; Brom has bound it again with a slat; it is twice its size; he cannot stand or hold a bowl on the night of the 290th. He knows what Oryn said it would cost. He gave his name, rank and office at the yard hatch on the 285th and was not written. He has apologised to Seln and been told to be nobody. He has asked for the wall to be entered and has been told that it is. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, that anything was taken from him, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does not know what the six in hoods hoped to see and has said that he does not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. Whether he heard Seln speak of the roof is not known.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:546:**Cleon.** Rune Path, Bronze; shown from outside only. He has said that he knows the hand; has shown the board; has said what bears, what is carried and what is nothing; has given the limit in both its parts; has said what being believed is to him and asked for a week (the 284th); has re-set that week to run from the 287th with his own page put by; has spoken his close; has Karis's name and has used it once. **He has taken no notice of Cael.** He does not know that anybody was set upon in the cut.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:630:- **The yard fire.** The stable's iron fire-basket on three legs, by the stall door; Brom's flint; upturned oak buckets; eight bowls ("I'd laid one for a mule before now"). Cleon comes in by the yard, having asked a keeper which street; he sits with his back half to the flame and eats half a bowl. Asked by Lira whether it is true: "I read how a thing's made… it's as old as it says it is… Whether he's told the truth in it, I can't say." His undertaking, to which Brom says "Good.": "That skin stays where it's lain… they'll not learn it from me." Brom's price: whatever was built was built over the whole country and down to every child; "Nobody spends so on a thing that he thinks is small… A price isn't a verdict… I'd want to hear the other side." After Lira's "You would have." she empties the old man's cold bowl into the pot and fills it hot. Cael does not write what he said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:638:**Where everyone is.** Five in the loft (Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln at the ladder's head) and Vastin in the end stall beneath. Cleon has gone back up through the blue gate; the leaf, the chronicle and the board are under the registry; the fifty-two sheets lie on their tables one night more. Oryn and the brown mule are between her fourth gate and her fifth. Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:650:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**; slat-bound; he rides the cart, sleeps in a stall, and takes the inner stair on his seat. He kept silent at the beam after one sentence. He heard the leaf; reached once aloud and was stopped; has stopped the same sentence in his own head; has said his piece at the fire (imperfect; the fault meant, which he called corrupt; aimed) and answered Lira ("I would have."). He was told across a dinner table that out here one counts who is owed a seat. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the sum, or what is under the bar. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:667:Movement 7 already carries the 294th, all-day list, twelve fragments, Karis's bound hand, Vastin day fifteen and no mule (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28–30`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:695:- **The march order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, **with Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one (watching her feet); Karis, the healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:699:- **What Oryn was told before she read him:** the two self-readings of the 281st and why; **the eleventh** (Vastin's, in the stair; he does not know); **the twelfth** (from "a man under the registry"; made things only; "Not a man."). Her ruling: nothing is turned "on my plank"; the road is his own.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:701:- **Dawn, the 299th.** "Twelve," … "And a mule." (Seln). The mule carries the three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis pinned a clean sheet to the hide's eastern edge, pricked the divider's point on it, and ruled the pencil line from the fourth ring through the point and a hand's breadth past ("I am not going to draw a stop that the paper does not give me").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:706:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial 316k; cold 98k; source-distance 190k (2 tracked passages; probe 1% / 12%); plan / canon / protected-text audit 744k tokens (REPAIR; seventy-six exact fixes). **Twenty-five applied by the coordinator** (the sixteen marker restorations, minimal, with the source's speakers; two sign-nouns; a broken join; three thaw intervals; the factor's seat cut), five of them amended. **Fifty-one DECLINED:** Vastin made to walk the whole road (the audit did not weigh closed Movement 6's knee); the ages re-derived from a printed date (date subtraction is reserved to the unspoken sum; the author softens the corner figure's claim instead); the Millrace count given to a "ford-keeper" (the woman with the net is locked Book 7's); the night exchange with Lira cut whole (only "You went stiff" is wrong; the author re-grounds it); "Twelve. And a mule." taken from Seln. **Repair r1 by the same author (claude-opus-5-5): seven joins written, the ages passage softened, Lira's knowledge re-grounded in his eyes, two tracked chains broken, a referent pass; Sol recheck CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES (two, both applied).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:746:- **Dawn (46:295–343):** unchanged. Seln: "Twelve. And a mule." Karis rules the line from the fourth ring over the join and a hand's breadth past the divider's prick, with the bound left hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:754:**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule, in file: Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with Cael at his left shoulder a stride back; Lira; the young one; Karis, the two healers and the brown mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Cleon is under Treswick with the leaf, the chronicle and the board. Pike is at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:766:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two new laths; the month as counted. He rode on the level and walked every hill, the cut and the notch. *"Here," and "Two words. Both of them ours." are his;* he stood on the leg once with the stick up. He kept and signed the tally. He sat before the six and laid no copper. He took Oryn's "Stand there." without a clause, gave her "Nineteen days," and stood an hour. He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee). *He put stake thirty-two back into the tarred case, which he carries.* He is on Teague's count as one of "your six"; that is a count for a contract; he has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. *The factor made him no offer.* He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the two words, the date, or what is under the bar; he knows that he is not told, and that it is "six people's".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:778:**Objects and money.** **130 → 128** (the 295th: the rope, two marks) **→ 127** (the 298th: meal and a flitch, one mark). Coppers are small money: Vastin's three to the dray's carter; the ferry's fare waived. The reserve sealed in the third box. The rope debt is paid. On the mule: three boxes, the flat, a sack of meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. With Karis: the hide with its pinned sheet, the Ternhall brass, her notebook, Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes, Vastin's copied page. With Cael: Hesk's book, the dividers shut in it, the fair copy of the leaf. With Vastin: the tarred kit case, *with stake thirty-two back in it, never driven*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:785:- **Inventory and order:** twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; Seln ahead, tall spear, Teague with Cael at his left a stride back, Lira, young one, Karis plus both healers and mule in the middle, Brom, Vastin a stride behind, bow last (`chapter-44.md:281–291`; `chapter-46.md:337–341`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:787:- **Teague's knowledge perimeter:** survey read and bearing; wall under a month; four ages and “three days past the iron.” His crew does not know leaf, list, mechanism, fragments, date, Vastin's former office, or the two inward words (`chapter-44.md:117–147,197–199`; `chapter-45.md:149–151`). Tall, bow and older healer still have not spoken to the six.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:793:- **Money/load:** purse 127; reserve sealed in third box; mule carries three boxes, flat, meal sack, Oryn's pannier and canvas; Cael carries fair leaf copy and dividers; Karis has hide/pinned sheet, notebook, Cleon roll, three-box sheet and Vastin copy (`chapter-45.md:283`; `chapter-46.md:303–307,321–335`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:803:- **Entry seam with Movement 7 ratified** (Sol plan audit): dawn of the 299th at Millrace ford; twelve and a mule in Teague's march order; the contract's ten; purse 127; Vastin day twenty, walking; Teague's wrist in linen; twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:804:- **The leg (the 299th–303rd).** The Stair's rim at noon on the 299th: Karis laid the kit's cord on the dead surveyor's figure (nine lengths and a piece, old iron to floor: "I am not checking the place; I am checking the cord"); her marker stone had been lifted and a turf relaid "since the thaw" (Seln: "Somebody has been round this place with a spade and made it agree with his sheet."). Teague began teaching Cael to read ground ("a piece of ground's a sum"; three things worth a fist: out of its place; stopped and ought to move; moving and ought to be stopped). **The cairn at noon on the 300th**, at the bend before the Hall's marsh, where a mule-path goes north over a saddle to three holds: **Oryn looked up it once and walked on east.** Her sum: Brom's shoulder wants a week of her eye (to the 305th), Vastin's knee is on her linen, and there is an edge twice any she has stood at; the three holds have had word ("a week, or more"). **Count her days past her road from this cairn** (one on the 301st … five on the 305th). She passed the chock-stones (locked Book 7's north fork) on the 302nd without a look. **Purse 123** (four marks at a hold's gate on the 300th: two skins, meal, a cheese, corn). A keeper said that a man on a bay had ridden through two days before and told him a crew would want water; two holds on the east road were barred at noon with nobody on the walk. No face, no name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:822:- **State at the night of the 305th:** twelve and the mule under the shale step; **thirteen fragments; deployment thirty-three; purse 123**; Vastin **twenty-six of thirty**; Oryn five days past her cairn; Teague's arm on a slat; two men on sticks. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 37,200 against 35,000, accepted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:831:- **The cairn (47:197–201).** At the bend where the carters' road swings south to the hold, a built cairn as high as a man's hip marks a mule-path that goes north over a saddle to "three gates"; it is not Book 7's heap of chock-stones, which is passed on the 302nd (48:109–117).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:833:- **The hold south of the cairn (47:205–233).** Four marks at its gate for two new water-skins, meal, a cheese and corn for the mule: **123**. Teague's four buy their own (a side of bacon). The keeper had skins filled and priced since the day before: a man on a bay rode through two days earlier, bought nothing, gave no name, and said that a crew would want them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:834:- **The Stair's bowl on the 299th (47:35–49; 47:53–81; 47:131).** (r1: the file's make-up is said once at 47:9–11 — twelve and a mule; six and a captain's four on a contract; two healers whom the count of ten leaves out.) Karis's grey stone is gone from between the two irons and a square of turf has been laid in its place with a spade, since the thaw; Seln: "There is one to a year." She sets another stone. Her number: the dead surveyor's *North station to floor*, nine lengths and a piece from the old iron to the grey's lip, which is also on the Stair's sheet in each of six years; laid with the kit's own cord from Vastin's case, by Karis, Lira and Seln, in an hour and ten minutes; "I am not checking the place; I am checking the cord." Cael does not touch it (a hundred and thirty-one days). Teague's three hold the rim unasked, the tall man on the spot where he stood in Book 7.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:837:- **Vastin on the leg.** He finds for himself how a stick keeps a file (47:11–13). At the hall's rise: "I have put my name to a good many papers which said that such a thing could not be … I am glad to have been spared the sight until I had left off signing" (47:265–271). His stick and the older healer's staff fall into one beat (48:23). At noon on the 303rd he says before he is asked that he will not stand a wall on day twenty-four, and that he does not know what he is for without it (49:33–49); Lira: "You can stand."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:838:- **The country east of the marsh (48:5; 48:9–39).** Every beck goes into the ground within a mile. Both living holds on the east road have their gates barred at noon and no head on the walk; the second lets down one bucket for the mule on a rope, for a copper. The dead hold's well is ten feet of steining on dry rubble: "That's what kills them, out here."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:839:- **The seep (48:131–143; 48:147–209; 48:213–285; 48:289–311).** A fold in the ridge's southern flank; a band of dark shale across it; a weeping ledge and a trodden pan under the band's western end; nineteen shale-backs, four of them calves. Teague: they lick the wet at first light and at dusk and mow along the band between; a Force shifted a block under a ledge herd on the cold road in Pike's time and "they found two mules" (this is Book 7's tale, with Teague now saying that he has stood where it was done). His rule for the fold: in by the west along the band's foot, never on the fall of the hill under a beast, two at a time, three steps and a stand, nobody steps quick near a calf. A skin takes more than six minutes at the drip. **The tall man stops the boy with a flat hand on the breastbone (48:197–209).** The read finds a bucket of water behind a loose leaf of shale; Pressure is wanted and refused; Brom draws the leaf with both arms; the tall man lifts his free hand from his knee and brings it down once. The old cow stands over them for the last skins. The mule drinks four skins from Oryn's canvas; the tall man and then the boy fetch four more at dusk; the bow takes one skin out of the boy's hand. Seln finds a keg's hoop and five made heels at the pan, the newest a week old: "a posting sends for its water."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:844:- **The fight's choreography inside the plan's four exchanges (50).** Positions: Seln in the grass above the path sixty yards east of the gap; the healers and the mule at the old ruts; nine at the shelf's mouth with Brom in front. *One:* two bolts on Iron under a buttoned coat — the breastbone and the left forearm; the neck and hands go "the colour of a slate that is drying after rain"; no sound. *Two:* Teague walks, since the Force wants three breaths of stillness; Cael keeps his left with the shortened watchman's stave from the alley (Seln's, handed over behind the brow) and takes the third stave across the left collar-bone without giving the stride; the tall man keeps the right with the ash crosswise and the steel high; both timbers and their trestles go a body's length back in one piece; five hoods go down; a crossbow's stock breaks under the lower baulk; nobody is under a timber; the wrist clicks and then the elbow. "Through" is Teague's, said to the place where the timbers stood (50:115–117). *Three:* the watch reforms behind the timbers where they lie, one bow spanned, the light relit; Teague cannot shut his right hand; he sees the width past the iron and asks Karis whether it is ground ("It is ground."). **(r1) Cael's entry, made in his head before a boot goes over, "in the tense that it would have to be true in afterward": *Nothing was gained inside.* (50:173–177; the sentence at 50:175). Teague then turns his head for the first time that morning and hands him the ground past the iron: "You've stood on three of them. I've stood on none. Say how." / "By count," said Cael (50:179–185).** Cael over first ("Grass"); Lira a stride in and a stride back ("Gone." / "Back. All of it." — "It's the same"); Karis; the boy when Teague looks at him; Vastin ("I am forbidden a wall. I am not, I think, forbidden to stand."). Sixty strides, two paces inside the iron; the watch's bow cannot turn without giving its side to Brom, the spear and the broad man's crossbow; the empty-handed man hauls back by the collar the one stave who starts for the iron. *The pinch:* eleven counts; **(r1) between two and three the empty-handed man calls "You'll die in there." across the iron, "as a person calls to a child on thin ice", and Cael answers "We've been in three times," for the crew that has stood on three such floors (50:253–259);** at four the watch's bowman looses at the broad man, the bolt takes his crossbow in the stock, his hip goes and a yard of rotten lip goes with it; Teague checks for half a stride and does not turn; the boy looks at Lira's boots and stays; at eleven the first stave is dropped and seven go through the gap singly. Seln counts seven through the gap and again over the second rise, a mile on (51:11).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:848:- **Teague's window (51:79–175).** He counts three by breathing and the spear by a shadow at the gap. The elbow has gone once before, "a long while ago, on a ledge". The bow to him: "And you never turned your head." / "If you'd turned, I'd have had something to say to you from the bottom of that hole"; "It's the good one"; of Oryn, "She asked me first. With my leg lying two ways." The boy asleep sitting, the dry cloth in his fist. Teague's reckoning: the boy "would go wherever he was looked at, a half-beat before he had seen what was there", and held at the grass by a girl's boots; "He would have to think about whose boots a boy watched." Of Cael: a left side kept with a stick and nothing else; "Teague could put that in a column." **Under the hide:** a sack and a half of meal, a bundle of bolts with no thread on their feathers, a mallet, a tarred cord knotted every few feet, and a dozen new bars, never driven, each stamped with two figures and the stroke and bar. He does not read it further; "It was not his to read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:856:- **The lamps finding's ground (52:161–221).** A ruled table kept since the Fallow: who crossed, what each carries, of what rank, and the stride; three ranks of Iron, a Copper, a Bronze, and since the 304th the boy and "a man who signed for other people's for forty years"; she has asked six people beside herself. The same stride for every one, whole, no dimming, back whole. After Vastin's stopped sentence and her rule she tears the ruled leaf out and carries it the length of the blanket to the corner farthest from the folded paper: "Two pages … Whoever wants a line from the one to the other will have to find something to rule it with." **Cael's third page** (52:213–221): the technician's sheet lies at the foot of the second row; he does not know to which corner it would lie the nearer, and keeps it off the wool. Nothing is said or written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:867:**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule in one camp under the step, at one fire in two halves: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man, the broad man, the young one, the older healer; Oryn and the brown mule. Seln is back from the gap and is to look again at first light; nobody moves until he has. Cleon is under Treswick. Pike is at Lowmarch. The watch's seven went east along the perimeter path on the morning of the 304th and have not been seen since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:871:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. The arm is an arm. She read the herd beside Teague, walked Cael in and out under it, went a stride over the fourth line and back ("It's the same"), stood in the row of five, and did not move her feet when the broad man fell. She coaches the boy and is watched by him. She knows the thirteenth and that Teague is not told; she saw the dry stance. She does not know the two words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:879:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty-six of thirty on the 305th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; he walked the whole leg in the file, a stride behind Brom. He said on the 303rd that he would not stand a wall and did not. **He stood inside the fourth line on the 304th, fifth of five; the sigil went out for the first time in his life and came back "to the grain".** He has said "Noted" a third time (to Karis's two pages). He began the sentence about the apparatus and the sigils and was stopped. He read the oldest row through, found the two slips, read both aloud, said that the objection came from the Compact, "part of it", knows both seals and has named neither; he drafted nothing. He made room for the broad man's stick. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the thirteenth, the two words, the date, or that the lean of the rows was seen. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:883:**Teague and his crew.** His right arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat; the wrist and the elbow went at the timbers; Oryn has warned him that a third time means a splint. He said "Noted" for the first time on the 303rd (to Cael's term) and a second time on the 304th (to Oryn). He handed Cael the ground past the iron ("Say how."). He did not turn when the broad man fell, and has told the broad man why. He thanked Cael for his left side. **He does not know that anything came to Cael at the timbers.** He knows what lies under the watch's hide and has left the reading of it to Karis. The broad man: right shin knit and bound to a board; a trestle's leg for a stick; his crossbow's stock split; he has said "Aye" to Vastin and to Oryn and nothing else to any of the six. The tall man has said nothing to any of them; he stopped the boy with a hand at the seep, kept Teague's right at the timbers, cut the stick. The young one: stepped over stake thirty-four fourth ("Four"), stood at the pinch, held when the broad man fell, ran when he might; he walked the seep at dusk. The older healer has spoken to none of the six; she set the shin and nodded once to Oryn. **Teague's four have seen:** five people stand inside the line and come out whole; a boy with a stick. **They have not been told:** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf, the list, the lamps finding, the two slips, the date, who Vastin was, or the doctrine "behind it". No wall has been drilled or stood.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:887:**Objects and money.** **127 → 123** (the 300th: four marks at a hold's gate for two water-skins, meal, a cheese and corn). No other spending from the purse. Coppers, kept apart from it as the closed text keeps them: one for the mule's bucket on the 301st; three of Brom's own on the watch's keg. The reserve is sealed in the third box. On the mule: three boxes (the fifty-two sheets, with fourteen of them and the nine new ones handled on the 305th and put back), the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. With Karis: the hide with its pinned sheet (the prick now ringed with a thumbnail, uninked), the Ternhall brass, her notebook (the torn lamps leaf in its back), Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes, Vastin's copied page, nine sheets of the piers. With Cael: Hesk's book, the dividers shut in it, the fair copy of the leaf (laid on the blanket folded and returned). With Vastin: the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two, never driven; the cord was used at the Stair by Karis and put back). The two slips are pinned again under the knot of the oldest row's tape, in the flat. Left at the watch's post: its hut, fire, keg, meal, bolts, mallet, cord, a dozen new bars, a sound crossbow on the baulk, a stave. Ten water-skins between the crews (two bought on the 300th).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:902:- **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She does NOT yet know of the thirteenth or of what it would cost his ribs (coordinator ruling), and does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:904:- **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).

